menu "Eye Demo Configuration"

config EYE_DEMO_ENABLE_CAMERA
    bool "Enable camera (DVP + OV2640) capture path"
    default y
    help
        Enables esp_video_init() + V4L2 DVP capture in eye_camera_init().
        When disabled, eye_camera_init() is a runtime no-op: the camera
        task never starts, no blob events are injected into urbi, and
        the display blits a static fill (or whatever the last frame was).
        Button + reactive runtime + urbi VM still run unaffected.

        Disable this on hardware where esp_video / esp32-camera /
        i2c_new_master_bus crashes inside ESP-IDF's interrupt allocator
        (see docs/urbi-embedded-design-risks.md "S3 + IDF v6 i2c intr_alloc
        incompatibility" for the open vendor issue and affected silicon).

endmenu
